AIM
To write a Python program using inheritance to calculate an electricity bill by creating a parent class PARENT and a child class Child.

ALGORITHM

Step 1: Start.
Step 2: Create a parent class named PARENT with two attributes.
Step 3: Define a method in the parent class to display the two attributes.
Step 4: Create a child class named Child that inherits from the parent class.
Step 5: Get customer details and electricity units as input.
Step 6: Check whether the electricity units are negative. If negative, display an error message.
Step 7: Otherwise, calculate the electricity bill based on the units consumed.
Step 8: Display the customer details and total bill amount.
Step 9: Create an object of the Child class.
Step 10: Call the parent class method and the electricity bill method.
Step 11: Stop.


